IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fhog-grant`

-- First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) -- worked cases, from the seat of the first home buyer.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case, a Revenue WA ruling or the Commissioner's guidance. The First Home Owner Grant Regulations 2000
-- (deposited) supply the cap (r 6) and the interest rate (r 8(3)).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table (scratchpad gen_wa_first-home-owner-grant-act-2000_baseline.py). Expected results were written by hand from the text.

`a clean history` MEANS History WITH
    `was a party to another application on which a grant was paid` IS FALSE
    `held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` IS FALSE
    `held a relevant interest in residential property before the commencement date` IS FALSE
    `occupied that property as a residence before 1 July 2004` IS FALSE
    `longest continuous months occupying that property from 1 July 2004` IS 0

`a history with a grant received` MEANS History WITH
    `was a party to another application on which a grant was paid` IS TRUE
    `held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` IS FALSE
    `held a relevant interest in residential property before the commencement date` IS FALSE
    `occupied that property as a residence before 1 July 2004` IS FALSE
    `longest continuous months occupying that property from 1 July 2004` IS 0

`a history with a home lived in for 2 years` MEANS History WITH
    `was a party to another application on which a grant was paid` IS FALSE
    `held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` IS FALSE
    `held a relevant interest in residential property before the commencement date` IS TRUE
    `occupied that property as a residence before 1 July 2004` IS FALSE
    `longest continuous months occupying that property from 1 July 2004` IS 24

`a history with an investment flat never lived in` MEANS History WITH
    `was a party to another application on which a grant was paid` IS FALSE
    `held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` IS FALSE
    `held a relevant interest in residential property before the commencement date` IS TRUE
    `occupied that property as a residence before 1 July 2004` IS FALSE
    `longest continuous months occupying that property from 1 July 2004` IS 0

`a history with a home lived in for 5 months` MEANS History WITH
    `was a party to another application on which a grant was paid` IS FALSE
    `held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` IS FALSE
    `held a relevant interest in residential property before the commencement date` IS TRUE
    `occupied that property as a residence before 1 July 2004` IS FALSE
    `longest continuous months occupying that property from 1 July 2004` IS 5

`a history with a home held before 1 July 2000` MEANS History WITH
    `was a party to another application on which a grant was paid` IS FALSE
    `held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` IS TRUE
    `held a relevant interest in residential property before the commencement date` IS FALSE
    `occupied that property as a residence before 1 July 2004` IS FALSE
    `longest continuous months occupying that property from 1 July 2004` IS 0

`Liam, as Chloe's partner` MEANS Partner WITH
    `is married to me on the commencement date` IS FALSE
    `the Commissioner is satisfied we live apart for good` IS FALSE
    `lives with me in a de facto relationship on the commencement date` IS TRUE
    `years we have lived together on that basis` IS 1
    `their history` IS `a clean history`

`Chloe, as Liam's partner` MEANS Partner WITH
    `is married to me on the commencement date` IS FALSE
    `the Commissioner is satisfied we live apart for good` IS FALSE
    `lives with me in a de facto relationship on the commencement date` IS TRUE
    `years we have lived together on that basis` IS 1
